The ULX3S's on-board ESP32 (as read through passthru.v):
  ESP32 with PSRAM ("ESP32 module (spiram)", ~4 MB heap), 4 MB flash, MicroPython v1.14
  (2021-02-02, the version esp32ecp5 recommends) with only the default boot.py (no esp32ecp5
  files on the filesystem), CPU at 160 MHz, unique id c88541c9c368.

Board revision: the pins behave like ULX3S v3.1.6+ (emard/ulx3s doc/constraints/prototype/
ulx3s_v316.lpf): wifi_en = J5, wifi_gpio0 = F1 (wifi_en on v3.0.x), wifi_gpio22 = L2
(wifi_gpio0 on v3.0.x). The LiteX platform and passthru.v use the v3.0.x pins, so here F1 drove
GPIO0 (it followed RTS through the EN logic) and L2 drove GPIO22: that is why esptool's reset
failed. The official flow (emard/ulx3s-passthru, ulx3s_v20_passthru_wifi.vhd): DTR/RTS -> EN/GPIO0
as in passthru.v, BTN0 also holds GPIO0 low, GPIO2 (sd_d0) low while entering programming;
then esptool / Arduino ("WEMOS LOLIN32") on the USB serial port.
The sampler gateware also drives L2 low ("wifi_gpio0"), which on this board is GPIO22.

Official ESP32 software: esp32ecp5 (MicroPython): ecp5.prog / ecp5.flash, FTP server (put x.bit
fpga | flash@0x... | sd@0x...), SD over SPI, WebREPL. The ESP32 reaches the FPGA's JTAG directly
(tms=5 tck=18 tdi=23 tdo=34), so it can program SRAM / config flash whatever bitstream runs.

Tools here:
  esp.sh <esptool args>   builds/loads the pass-through into the FPGA's SRAM, runs esptool
  esptool_ftdi.py         esptool over pyftdi (the FT231X is in bit-bang mode after
                          openFPGALoader); classic DTR/RTS reset instead of the tty-only one
  boot_log.py             reset + print what the ESP32 says at 115200
The MicroPython REPL works through the pass-through at 115200.
The ESP32 firmware must never touch the SD pins (GPIO2/4/12/13/14/15) while the FPGA owns the
card, nor GPIO16/17 (PSRAM) or drive GPIO5 (TMS) early after boot.
